==English==

===Etymology===
From the {{etyl|la|en}} {{m|la|sine||without}} + {{m|la|diē}}, the ablative singular of {{m|la|diēs||a day}}. Literally meaning "without a day".

===Pronunciation===
* {{a|UK}} {{IPA|/ˈsʌɪni ˈdʌɪiː/|lang=en}}

===Adverb===
{{en-adv|-}}

# [[without|Without]] [[specifying]] a [[date]] (for a [[future]] [[event]]); [[indefinitely]].
#* '''1979''', {{w|André Brink}}, ''A Dry White Season'', Vintage 1998, p. 105:
#*: In anticipation of Dr Hassiem's release the inquest of Mr Ngubene's death, originally scheduled for 13 April, was postponed '''''sine die'''''.

